    "result_text": "The full build passed (exit 0), with the only test class being `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 all 3 tests green, no failures or errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization on owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- **New `canonicalAddress(String)` helper** \u2014 trims, collapses internal whitespace runs to a single space, upper-cases, then expands whole-token street abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`) via an `ADDRESS_ABBREVIATIONS` map. It's `null`-safe and idempotent, so it can safely be applied to already-stored values during comparison.\n- **`normalizeAddress(OwnerFieldsDto)`** writes the canonical form back onto the request, run **first** in `addOwner` \u2014 before `validateRequiredFields`. This makes the required-field check reject an address that is blank after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"` \u2192 `\"\"` \u2192 400), and ensures the stored and returned `address` is the normalized value.\n- **Address comparisons** in `rejectDuplicateHousehold` and `assignHousehold` (both membership matching and the shared `householdId` derivation) now use `canonicalAddress(...)` instead of the old case/whitespace-only `normalizeForComparison`, so every address comparison uses the normalized form. `lastName` still uses `normalizeForComparison`.\n\nBehavior verified by the acceptance tests: `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`, `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`, and blank-after-normalize \u2192 400.",
